  "notes": [
    "The example schema ids are test contracts, not type-identity hashing or a schema registry.",
    "Text JSON only for authoring test metadata; actual transport bytes are the MessagePack hex vectors.",
    "No class/enum/Option/Result arbitrary codecs or actor serializer integration are claimed.",
    "Golden byte vectors generated independently with Python msgpack packb(use_bin_type=True) + hashlib.sha256 on canonical descriptors; schema-v2 format is intentionally incompatible with v1.",
    "Decoder rejects noncanonical integer/string/array header encodings and untrusted array length budgets before allocation.",
    "New boundary vectors exercise i64 minimum/maximum, UTF-8 multibyte scalars, negative zero bit preservation, and empty tuple framing.",
    "Numeric i64 extremes are represented as strings in JSON metadata to preserve 64-bit integer precision; payload is encoded as canonical signed i64 MessagePack."
  ]
